\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids in Columbia County has 75 years on record, and August to September came in under 90% of normal in 38 of them. In 2025, September to October ran 61% of normal and October to November ran 56% on the middle of the grids. So far in 2026, May to June came in at 63% and June to July at 75%. Every grid had its driest year in 1958, with grid 28363 at 54%.</p>"}
